 when kevin attacks his  brother for eating his pizza totally  justified which causes complete  pandemonium and everyone in the house  hating him look what you did you little  jerk we care about kevin because which  one of us hasn't been in a situation  where we feel ignored or unloved by our  family this is what makes the ending so  powerful when we see how much kevin and  his family truly love one another the  scene also has the added bonus of  setting up why kevin's dad doesn't have  his son's passport or airplane ticket it  got covered in spilt milk and  accidentally thrown in the trash in home  sweet home alone there is no such scene  you just have a bratty kid who doesn't  like his family but i just don't see why  we have to share our house with every  stupid relative we have one of the  biggest differences between these two  movies is the setup mainly in terms of  how these two kids get left home alone  and why they don't go for help and let  me tell you in the age of cell phones  and the internet home sweet home alone  has to perform some cirque du soleil  level mental gymnastics for us to  believe max could possibly be left home  alone in the original it's pretty simple  a storm has blown out the power the  family is late for their flight to  france and they forget kevin  in the new version we find out that  they're traveling to japan for some  reason and that the day before their  flight the family had to be split up  into two separate flights in the  pandemonium of them leaving in their  ubers they forget max who fell asleep  watching cartoons in the back seat of  their car in the garage and all i'm  thinking about is how short this movie  would be if he got carbon monoxide  poisoning max's uncle thinks that max  must have gotten on that earlier flight  with his mom but that's not the case and  when max finds out he is home alone he  lives it up just like kevin in the  original even dressing up as a woman now  i personally don't have anything against  that who among us hasn't put on our  mom's heels from time to time but bold  move disney i guess the movie can't air  in china anymore  i should also mention that max doesn't  have a cell phone and can't access the  internet through the movie's version of  an alexa because it's programmed in  german he also refuses to go get help  from his neighbors or the police because  he believes that his parents will go to  jail if the police find out they left  him home alone but moving on to the main  catalyst of the story and why i think  pam and jeff are the main characters the  whole story centers around them having  to move out of their home because they  can't pay the bills but when jeff finds  out a creepy antique doll of his mothers  could sell for two hundred thousand  dollars it just might be the financial  christmas miracle they've been looking  for this is where max comes into play  who winds up at the mackenzie's open  house when he really had to use their  washroom there he finds jeff's doll  collection and when the doll goes  missing jeff and pam assume it was max  who took it starting the events of home  sweet home alone where they need to  break into the house and get their doll  back this is what really separates jeff  and pam from harry and mar harry and  marv are just bad people looking to make  a quick buck the film portrays jeff and  pam as this wholesome family down on  their luck unable to buy nice christmas  presents for their children hell they  even volunteer at singing for seniors  the break-in isn't really like harry and  mars it's more to reclaim what was  already theirs so unlike home loan where  you're rooting for kevin to kick the  [ __ ] out of the bad guys with his booby  traps it just kind of feels weird that  max is doing the same thing to these  really nice people who are trying to  save their family the most blatant  crossover between the two films is the  introduction of buzz mcallister kevin's  brother he's all grown up now working  for the police force and kevin is the  owner of mcallister home security which  max's house has buzz really hasn't  changed much no it's been able to obtain  this wild stallion in fact he's only in  two or three scenes he's pretty much the  worst cop around because when he gets a  call that there's a boy home alone he  thinks it's just his brother playing a  prank on him and decides not to look  into it shame on you i also don't know  why the mom and max are british maxwell  johann mercer maybe it was a casting  thing now when max's mom does find out  that they left max home alone there's  only one ticket left to america and she  goes by herself just like katherine  o'hara's character in the original  unfortunately there's no john candy in a  pokeband there's this guy she meets in  the plane but he's totally annoying also  that fake movie kevin watches angels  with filthy souls has gone from film  noir to whatever the hell this sci-fi  monstrosity is and it wouldn't be  christmas without church right in home  alone kevin uses the manger to hide  himself from the burglars and while max  doesn't use the manger like kevin does  it reminds him of his family but it's  the addition of a toy drive which is new  in this version now max like kevin comes  from a very wealthy family yet still  ends up taking a toy from the toy drive  and there's no scene in the church where  max learns not to judge a book by its  cover with the old man it just kinda  ends there there is a choir though so  jeff and pam see max at the church and  decide now is the opportunity to strike  while he's not at home it's perfect  we go now while they're not home and get  our doll back and literally the next  scene they get there and decide to wait  until dark defeating their entire  purpose for leaving we'll wait till it  gets dark and this film is jam-packed  with product placement especially for  kellogg's products like max walks around  with a backpack of fruit loops for some  reason all the time and there are  pop-tarts everywhere i mean the original  did have some with pepsi and frito-lays  but this was pretty distracting speaking  of foods there's a cool easter egg at  pam and jeff's house with little nero's  pizza the same company kevin and his  family order from now we get to what  everyone's come here for the traps  unlike the original the first few traps  that jeff and pam succumb to aren't  created by the kid at all they fall into  an icy pool struggle to get over a stone  wall which jeff then crashes into a  dollhouse thing all of these are just  because they're stupid and not because  of max's ingenuity but then we get to  the booby trap plan kevin has his mapped  out on a piece of paper while max has  written his in chalk on the wall this  was always one of my favorite parts in  the film the creating traps montage and  home sweet home has this too but makes  the tragic mistake of intercutting the  trap making process with these  insufferable singing clips  [Music]  it just takes away from the energy going  into the film's final act now i gotta  say that there were some pretty  ingenious traps in this new version some  of my favorites included a race car  attached to a firecracker which lights  pam's feet on fire the thumbtack nerf  gun or the icicle indiana jones run but  for every cool one there are some  definite misfires like the cookies left  out for santa that jeff eats which were  made of hot sauce the vr machine which  jeff thinks he's actually on a mountain  ledge or stepping on legos which just  don't have the same impact like when  marv stepped on the christmas ornaments  there's also a lot of cgi like this cgi  pack of sugar that's flung at them the  cold breath is cgi and the snow is fake  i'm just a fan of more of the practical  effects like the paint canisters falling  off the second floor in the original  here they've been replaced by flour and  milk and jeff and pam really get put  through some torture but the film  decides to remind us what they're here  for don't you dare judge me  i'm doing this for my family why show us  them getting their [ __ ] knocked out of  them and then remind us that they're  doing this just to save their families  home there are also some memorable lines  that are rehashed for fan service like  this line you guys give up or you're  thirsty for more but in the new version  it feels like it was added in  post-production as an afterthought given  up yet  as jeff and pam finally corner max in  the film's climax we basically learned  the whole thing was just a  misunderstanding max thought they had  come to steal him when all they wanted  was this doll back so he goes from  nearly killing them to staying over at  their place until his mom comes home if  we had known  you were staying here by yourself we  would have handled things a lot  differently  yeah that's the ending well kinda it  turns out that jeff's nephew had the  doll the whole time and for some reason  he decides to chuck it in the middle of  the air almost destroying it but max  ends up catching it and saving the day  [Laughter]  so no one gets arrested like harry and  marv do and jeff and pam learn the moral  of the story because i guess home is  just another word for family right but  stop right there unlike the original we  fast forward one year the mckenzies have  used the money from the sale of the doll  to get their life back on track and now  max and his family seem to have ditched  that whole other family that came to  tokyo with them and are now spending it  with the mercers  obviously this video has no bias in it  at all but i want to hear your thoughts  on which home alone reigns supreme in  the comments below thank you for  watching be sure to like and subscribe  and for more bad takes you can follow me  on twitter and instagram at thingstoryt  until next time remember daddy loves you  very much  you

